a packaged step written by someone else.

4
00:00:18,115 --> 00:00:19,425
Two questions about it.

5
00:00:19,765 --> 00:00:24,323
First: what does v4 name? It names
a tag in someone else's repository.

6
00:00:24,363 --> 00:00:28,199
A tag is a name for one commit
that isn't expected to move.

7
00:00:28,239 --> 00:00:32,075
But a tag can be moved by whoever
controls that repository.

8
00:00:32,115 --> 00:00:37,001
So the code your job runs tomorrow is
whatever that tag points at tomorrow.

9
00:00:37,341 --> 00:00:42,629
Second: since the twenty-third of September
2026, Node 24 is the only JavaScript

10
00:00:42,669 --> 00:00:48,024
action runtime on github.com runners. The
runtime is the program that executes an

11
00:00:48,064 --> 00:00:53,219
action's code. An older major version of
an action that declares Node 20 isn't

12
00:00:53,259 --> 00:00:58,814
rejected. According to the runner's source
it's executed on Node 24, a configuration

13
00:00:58,854 --> 00:01:00,412
its authors didn't test.

14
00:01:00,752 --> 00:01:05,436
So that one line now runs code you didn't
choose on a runtime its authors didn't

15
00:01:05,476 --> 00:01:09,865
test, and it still shows green. This
video is about taking control of both.

16
00:01:09,905 --> 00:01:14,353
