flavor. Say it out loud.

208
00:16:06,506 --> 00:16:12,460
By the rules: workflows 3 and 6 both filter
on tags that match v*, so both start.

209
00:16:12,500 --> 00:16:18,454
And the image gets 0.2.0 from the semver
rule, sha-6fe5455 from the sha rule, and

210
00:16:18,494 --> 00:16:24,596
latest from the default flavor. That's
derived from the documentation, and Lab 26.6

211
00:16:24,636 --> 00:16:26,224
is where you check it.

212
00:16:26,564 --> 00:16:34,055
Step 3: the artifact, consumed. Replay
labs/run ch20a/lab-26-7-artifact.

213
00:16:34,095 --> 00:16:41,482
You saw it in video 146. Look at it
now as the last step of workflow 7.

214
00:16:41,822 --> 00:16:45,994
On a runner, the commit and the ref lines
would carry the run's values, and the two

215
00:16:46,034 --> 00:16:48,785
files would be the ones the
download step placed there.

216
00:16:49,125 --> 00:16:54,025
Two guards in the script, two in the workflow.
The script refuses an empty directory

217
00:16:54,065 --> 00:16:58,084
and an unknown environment. The
workflow refuses an empty upload with

218
00:16:58,124 --> 00:17:02,554
if-no-files-found: error, and the download
action refuses a digest mismatch.

219
00:17:02,894 --> 00:17:07,258
On your practice repository, in your
normal shell. The interface changes.

220
00:17:07,298 --> 00:17:10,877
The lab text and the linked
documentation are the reference.

221
00:17:10,917 --> 00:17:13,592
No GitHub output was
captured by the authors.

222
00:17:13,932 --> 00:17:17,931
Lab 26.6. Add workflow 6 on a
branch and open a pull request.

223
00:17:17,971 --> 00:17:23,427
Don't merge yet. Predict: is the login step
executed, is anything pushed, and which

224
00:17:23,467 --> 00:17:27,068
tags does the metadata step
produce for a pull request?

225
00:17:27,108 --> 00:17:32,431
Then open the run and look at the login
step's status, and at the job summary for

226
00:17:32,471 --> 00:17:33,027
the tags.

227
00:17:33,367 --> 00:17:38,103
After merging, read the run for the push
to main, and compare the tags with your

228
00:17:38,143 --> 00:17:42,939
prediction from the two Git values. Then
push the version tag, list the runs, and

229
00:17:42,979 --> 00:17:47,835
see which workflows started. Find the
package on your organization's page and look

230
00:17:47,875 --> 00:17:49,029
at its list of tags.

231
00:17:49,369 --> 00:17:54,817
Lab 26.7. Add workflow 7, and after the
run, open the run's summary page and find

232
00:17:54,857 --> 00:17:59,425
the artifact with its name, and the
place where its digest is shown.

233
00:17:59,465 --> 00:18:04,100
In the second job's log, compare the
digest that was printed with it.

234
00:18:04,140 --> 00:18:09,792
Then start one run by hand: gh workflow run
is 🟡 CAUTION, since it starts a run that

235
00:18:09,832 --> 00:18:13,316
uses minutes and may deploy
if the workflow deploys.

236
00:18:13,356 --> 00:18:14,942
This one only simulates.

237
00:18:16,782 --> 00:18:18,430
Five mistakes to watch for.

238
00:18:18,770 --> 00:18:22,806
A job-level permissions block that
names only the extra permission.

239
00:18:22,846 --> 00:18:27,915
Root cause: the job-level block replaces
the workflow-level one, so every permission

240
00:18:27,955 --> 00:18:30,896
not named becomes none,
including contents: read.

241
00:18:31,236 --> 00:18:37,227
Writing @v10 for astral-sh/setup-uv. Root
cause: that action has no floating major

242
00:18:37,267 --> 00:18:38,698
tag since version 8.

243
00:18:39,038 --> 00:18:43,913
Deploying by the image tag main or latest.
Root cause: both are names that move;

244
00:18:43,953 --> 00:18:46,187
they do not identify what was tested.

245
00:18:46,527 --> 00:18:51,508
Deleting a Git tag to undo a release. Root
cause: the tag push already started the

246
00:18:51,548 --> 00:18:56,651
workflows with a matching filter, and deleting
the tag does not unpublish the image.

247
00:18:56,991 --> 00:19:01,072
Leaving an old action major in
place because the run is green.

248
00:19:01,112 --> 00:19:06,589
Root cause: an action that declares Node
20 is executed on Node 24, a configuration

249
00:19:06,629 --> 00:19:08,251
its authors did not test.

250
00:19:10,091 --> 00:19:15,453
Now, out of the lab. A team that serves
models has a release workflow written in

251
00:19:15,493 --> 00:19:19,977
2024. It references actions by major
tag and runs on ubuntu-latest.

252
00:19:20,017 --> 00:19:25,649
In the autumn of 2026 two things happen
within weeks, and neither is a commit to the

253
00:19:25,689 --> 00:19:31,051
repository. On the twenty-third of September,
Node 20 stops being available, and

254
00:19:31,091 --> 00:19:36,723
their older action majors are executed on
Node 24. Between the nineteenth of October

255
00:19:36,763 --> 00:19:42,057
and the nineteenth of November, by the
schedule GitHub announced, ubuntu-latest

256
00:19:42,097 --> 00:19:43,745
migrates to Ubuntu 26.04.

257
00:19:44,085 --> 00:19:48,934
If a release then fails, the team has
nothing to bisect: the repository didn't

258
00:19:48,974 --> 00:19:51,880
change. That's the cost
of floating references.

259
00:19:52,220 --> 00:19:57,327
Apply the model. Pin each action to a
commit ID with the version as a comment, on

260
00:19:57,367 --> 00:20:02,538
the Node 24 majors. Name the runner image.
Let Dependabot propose the pin updates.

261
00:20:02,578 --> 00:20:07,876
From then on each of those changes arrives
as a pull request with a diff, a run, and

262
00:20:07,916 --> 00:20:09,084
a commit to revert.

263
00:20:10,924 --> 00:20:17,208
Your turn. Do Lab 26.6, "Workflow 6,
build and push a container image", in

264
00:20:17,248 --> 00:20:22,422
lab-manual/m26-actions-fundamentals.md,
in your normal shell.

265
00:20:22,762 --> 00:20:27,705
Three predictions, written down before each
run. For the pull request: whether the

266
00:20:27,745 --> 00:20:32,810
login step runs and which tags are computed.
For the push to main: the tags from the

267
00:20:32,850 --> 00:20:37,855
branch name and the short commit ID. For
the version tag: which workflows start and

268
00:20:37,895 --> 00:20:39,313
which image tags appear.

269
00:20:39,653 --> 00:20:45,429
The challenge is Lab 26.7, "Workflow 7,
create an artifact and consume it", in the

270
00:20:45,469 --> 00:20:46,139
same file.

271
00:20:49,979 --> 00:20:54,704
Answer out loud. A strong answer explains
what a tag is and who can move it, and

272
00:20:54,744 --> 00:20:58,279
what a commit ID gives you that
a tag doesn't, in Git terms.

273
00:20:58,319 --> 00:21:02,747
It says how the pin is kept current so
that pinning doesn't become neglect.

274
00:21:03,087 --> 00:21:07,826
For the second half it states the date,
what happens to an action that declares the

275
00:21:07,866 --> 00:21:11,166
older runtime, and what the
rule for a workflow author is.

276
00:21:11,206 --> 00:21:15,830
The follow-up asks what still moves under
a workflow when every action is pinned.

277
00:21:15,870 --> 00:21:18,594
Use the pinned-or-floating
list from this video.

278
00:21:20,434 --> 00:21:21,362
Let's land this.

279
00:21:21,702 --> 00:21:23,362
You should now be able to say:

280
00:21:23,702 --> 00:21:28,802
Workflow 6 builds on every pull request
without logging in, and pushes from main and

281
00:21:28,842 --> 00:21:32,045
from version tags, with tags
computed from Git facts.

282
00:21:32,385 --> 00:21:37,544
An image tag is a name: sha- plus the
commit ID names a commit, main and latest

283
00:21:37,584 --> 00:21:39,979
move, a version comes from a Git tag.

284
00:21:40,319 --> 00:21:45,222
Workflow 7 builds once, uploads an artifact,
and deploys exactly the downloaded

285
00:21:45,262 --> 00:21:46,911
files, with a digest check.

286
00:21:47,251 --> 00:21:52,142
Actions are pinned by commit ID because a
tag can be moved; Dependabot proposes the

287
00:21:52,182 --> 00:21:52,617
updates.

288
00:21:52,957 --> 00:21:59,989
Node 24 is the only JavaScript action runtime
since 23 September 2026; use the Node

289
00:22:00,029 --> 00:22:03,142
24 majors, and name the runner image.

290
00:22:04,982 --> 00:22:12,489
Read the rest of section 20A.13 and
sections 20A.14 to 20A.18 of Chapter 20A.

291
00:22:12,529 --> 00:22:15,527
Do the Practice section 20A.20.

